window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-954c69856eb43359"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"create-browser-based-games\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">创建浏览器游戏</h1> <p>先定义游戏计划，再让 Codex 在真实浏览器中构建和测试。</p> <p>让 Codex 先把游戏构想整理成清晰计划，再创建真正可运行的浏览器游戏。使用 ImageGen 生成视觉素材，并让 Codex 在真实浏览器中测试游戏、反复调整操作方式和界面。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>从零开始构建浏览器游戏。</li> <li>需要反复测试和调整操作、视觉效果与部署方式的游戏项目。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/playwright-interactive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$playwright（需联网）</a></td> <td>在真实浏览器中游玩，检查当前状态，并针对实际构建结果不断调整操作方式、节奏和界面体验。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$imagegen</code></td> <td>生成概念图、精灵图、背景和界面素材，并保留可复用的提示词，以便后续素材批次保持一致。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/openai-docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$openai-docs（需联网）</a></td> <td>在为游戏接入 OpenAI 功能之前，查阅当前官方指南。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Web 游戏技术栈</td> <td><a href=\"https://nextjs.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Next.js（需联网）</a> 搭配 <a href=\"https://phaser.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phaser（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://pixijs.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PixiJS（需联网）</a></td> <td>适合作为浏览器游戏界面和渲染层的实用默认方案。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>后端技术栈</td> <td><a href=\"https://fastify.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fastify（需联网）</a>、WebSockets、<a href=\"https://www.postgresql.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Postgres（需联网）</a> 和 <a href=\"https://redis.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Redis（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果游戏需要持久化、匹配玩家、排行榜或发布/订阅功能，这是一个稳健的默认方案。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建之前先规划游戏</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $playwright-interactive、$imagegen 和 $openai-docs，在这个代码库中规划并构建浏览器游戏。\n\n实现 PLAN.md，并将工作记录在 `.logs/` 下。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">使用 AGENTS.md 编写自定义指令</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">简介</h2> <p>构建游戏最能体现 Codex 不只是生成代码。真正的游戏通常需要明确的构想、渲染层、前端外壳、后端状态、素材制作，以及持续不断的视觉调优</p> <p>如果先让 Codex 明确写下游戏的具体设计，再使用 Playwright Interactive 在真实浏览器中测试并不断调整，这种方式通常最有效。</p> <p><a id=\"start-with-the-game-plan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">从游戏计划开始</h2> <p>在 Codex 搭建任何内容之前，先让它创建 <code>PLAN.md</code>，把游戏设计写具体：</p> <ul> <li>玩家目标</li> <li>核心循环</li> <li>输入方式和操作</li> <li>胜利与失败条件</li> <li>进度或难度设计</li> <li>视觉方向</li> <li>技术栈和托管假设</li> <li>里程碑顺序</li> </ul> <p>仅仅说“做一个游戏”过于含糊。Codex 需要知道每个部分应如何实现，并且在构建过程中通常需要反复参照这些实现细节，因此这份计划很重要。</p> <p>你可以通过 <code>/plan</code> 斜杠命令启用计划模式。 将生成的内容保存到 <code>PLAN.md</code> 文件中。</p> <p><a id=\"guide-codexs-behavior-with-agentsmd\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"agentsmd-codex\">使用 AGENTS.md 指导 Codex</h2> <p>为了确保 Codex 遵循计划、验证工作并使用合适的工具，请编写类似下面的 <code>AGENTS.md</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\"># Game name\n\n&lt;Type of game&gt;\n\nTech Stack:\n\n- NextJS for frontend (hosted on Vercel)\n- &lt;insert technology&gt; for rendering\n- Fastify for backend, websockets (hosted on &lt;hosting platform&gt;)\n- Postgres for database (hosted on &lt;hosting platform&gt;)\n- Redis for caching and pub/sub (hosted on &lt;hosting platform&gt;)\n- OpenAI for generative AI features\n\nTips:\n\n- Use build and test commands to verify your work as soon as you complete a feature or task\n- Use the PLAN.md file to guide your work when building new features\n- Log your work under .logs (create new log files as you see fit) to record your thought process and decisions, and reference them when iterating on features\n- Use playwright to test the visual output of your work, and iterate if it doesn't look right or fit the vibe\n- Use imagegen to generate visual assets for your work, and every time you generate a collection of assets, save the prompts you used to be able to continue generating more of the same assets later (create files in .prompts)\n- Use Context7 MCP to fetch &lt;rendering framework&gt; docs\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\"># 游戏名称\n\n&lt;Type of game&gt;\n\n技术栈：\n\n- 前端使用 NextJS（托管在 Vercel）\n- 渲染使用 &lt;insert technology&gt;\n- 后端和 websockets 使用 Fastify（托管在 &lt;hosting platform&gt;）\n- 数据库使用 Postgres（托管在 &lt;hosting platform&gt;）\n- 缓存与发布/订阅使用 Redis（托管在 &lt;hosting platform&gt;）\n- 生成式 AI 功能使用 OpenAI\n\n提示：\n\n- 每完成一项功能或任务，就尽快使用构建和测试命令验证工作结果\n- 构建新功能时，使用 PLAN.md 文件指导工作\n- 在 .logs 中记录工作（可按需要创建新的日志文件），记下思考过程和决定，并在迭代功能时参考这些记录\n- 使用 playwright 测试工作的视觉输出，如果效果不对或不符合整体氛围，就继续迭代\n- 使用 imagegen 生成视觉素材；每次生成一组素材时，都保存所用提示词，方便之后继续生成风格一致的素材（在 .prompts 中创建文件）\n- 使用 Context7 MCP 获取 &lt;rendering framework&gt; 文档</div></div> <p>这样 Codex 就能在较长时间内独立工作。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">使用技能复用工作模式</h2> <p>在 AGENTS.md 文件中提到的技能应添加到项目中：</p> <ul> <li>需要时使用 ImageGen 生成视觉素材。</li> <li>使用 Playwright Interactive 在真实浏览器中测试游戏，并不断调整操作方式。</li> <li>使用 OpenAI Docs 获取最新 OpenAI API 指南。</li> <li>还可以添加 Context7 MCP 服务器，以便获取渲染框架的最新文档。</li> </ul> <p>有关如何添加技能的更多信息，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能文档（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"let-codex-work-and-iterate\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">让 Codex 持续工作并迭代</h2> <p>Codex 会根据初始提示词生成游戏的第一个版本。</p> <p>如果有大量图像素材需要生成，第一个版本可能需要一段时间，有时甚至需要数小时。Codex 可以在真实浏览器中测试并调整游戏，因此无需你输入指令，也能持续推进很长时间。</p> <p>计划越明确，第一轮之后的最终效果通常越好。</p> <p>测试时，可以继续提出游戏玩法改动或视觉素材更新要求，并提供截图，直到你对结果满意为止。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"create-browser-based-games\">Create browser-based games</h1> <p>Define a game plan and let Codex build and test it in a live browser.</p> <p>Use Codex to turn a game brief into first a well-defined plan, and then a real browser-based game. Use imagegen to generate visual assets, and let Codex test the game in a live browser to iterate on controls and UI.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Building a browser-based game from scratch</li> <li>Game builds where controls, visuals, and deployment all need repeated testing and tuning</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/playwright-interactive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$playwright (online)</a></td> <td>Play the game in a live browser, inspect the current state, and iterate on controls, timing, and UI feel against the real build.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$imagegen</code></td> <td>Generate concept art, sprites, backgrounds, and UI assets, then keep the prompts reusable for later asset batches.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/openai-docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$openai-docs (online)</a></td> <td>Pull current official guidance before wiring OpenAI-powered features into the game.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Web game stack</td> <td><a href=\"https://nextjs.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Next.js (online)</a> with <a href=\"https://phaser.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phaser (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://pixijs.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PixiJS (online)</a></td> <td>A practical default for browser-based game UI plus the rendering layer.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Backend stack</td> <td><a href=\"https://fastify.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fastify (online)</a>, WebSockets, <a href=\"https://www.postgresql.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Postgres (online)</a>, and <a href=\"https://redis.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Redis (online)</a></td> <td>A strong default when the game needs persistence, matchmaking, leaderboards, or pub/sub.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Plan the Game Before You Build It</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $playwright-interactive, $imagegen, and $openai-docs to plan and build a browser game in this repo.\nImplement PLAN.md, and log your work under `.logs/`.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">Custom instructions with AGENTS.md</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Building a game is one of the clearest examples of where Codex helps with more than code generation. A real game usually needs a written concept, a rendering layer, frontend shell work, backend state, asset production, and constant visual tuning</p> <p>This use case works best when Codex starts by writing down exactly what the game should do, then iterates using Playwright interactive to test the game in a live browser.</p> <h2 id=\"start-with-the-game-plan\">Start with the game plan</h2> <p>Before Codex scaffolds anything, ask it to create a <code>PLAN.md</code> that defines the game in concrete terms:</p> <ul> <li>the player goal</li> <li>the main loop</li> <li>inputs and controls</li> <li>win and fail states</li> <li>progression or difficulty</li> <li>visual direction</li> <li>the stack and hosting assumptions</li> <li>the milestone order</li> </ul> <p>That plan matters because “build a game” is too vague on its own. Codex needs to know how to implement each part of the game, and often refer to the implementation details as it builds.</p> <p>You can activate plan mode with the <code>/plan</code> slash command. Take the output and save it to a <code>PLAN.md</code> file.</p> <h2 id=\"guide-codexs-behavior-with-agentsmd\">Guide Codex's behavior with AGENTS.md</h2> <p>To make sure Codex follows the plan, verifies its work and uses the right tools, define an <code>AGENTS.md</code> that looks like this:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\"># Game name\n\n&lt;Type of game&gt;\n\nTech Stack:\n\n- NextJS for frontend (hosted on Vercel)\n- &lt;insert technology&gt; for rendering\n- Fastify for backend, websockets (hosted on &lt;hosting platform&gt;)\n- Postgres for database (hosted on &lt;hosting platform&gt;)\n- Redis for caching and pub/sub (hosted on &lt;hosting platform&gt;)\n- OpenAI for generative AI features\n\nTips:\n\n- Use build and test commands to verify your work as soon as you complete a feature or task\n- Use the PLAN.md file to guide your work when building new features\n- Log your work under .logs (create new log files as you see fit) to record your thought process and decisions, and reference them when iterating on features\n- Use playwright to test the visual output of your work, and iterate if it doesn't look right or fit the vibe\n- Use imagegen to generate visual assets for your work, and every time you generate a collection of assets, save the prompts you used to be able to continue generating more of the same assets later (create files in .prompts)\n- Use Context7 MCP to fetch &lt;rendering framework&gt; docs\n</code></pre> <p>This allows Codex to run independently for a long time, and use the relevant skills as needed.</p> <h2 id=\"leverage-skills\">Leverage skills</h2> <p>Add the skills mentioned in the AGENTS.md file:</p> <ul> <li>Imagegen so Codex can generate visual assets for the game as needed</li> <li>Playwright interactive so Codex can test the game in a live browser</li> <li>OpenAI docs so Codex can fetch the latest OpenAI API documentation</li> <li>Optionally, you can add the Context7 MCP server to fetch the latest docs for the rendering framework</li> </ul> <p>Learn more about how to add skills in the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skills documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <p><strong>Tip</strong>: Ask Codex to save prompts for image generation in a file so that visual assets are all consistent. Give directions on the style of assets you want to generate, and let Codex come up with detailed reusable prompts.</p> <h2 id=\"let-codex-work-and-iterate\">Let Codex work and iterate</h2> <p>Codex will generate a first version of the game based on the initial plan.</p> <p>If you have a lot of image assets that need to be generated, this first version can take a while, sometimes several hours. Since Codex can test its work and try the game in a live browser, it can go on for a long time without any input.</p> <p>The more defined the plan, the better the final output after the first iteration.</p> <p>As you test it out, iterate as needed by providing screenshots, asking for gameplay changes or updates to visual assets, until you are happy with the result.</p>"};
